// games/sonic4/test/poison/poison_landing_early.emp — POISON (see README).
//
// TARGETS: check_landings' EARLY edge — a burst that starts before horizontal blanking
//          opens, i.e. in active display (substrate item 1c).
// EXPECTED FRAGMENT: "EARLIER than the earliest legal"
//
// Two one-word CRAM ops in ONE fire. Every structural guard passes: two ops is inside
// the ceiling of four, two stream ops is exactly the ceiling of two, and two words is
// inside its class's burst ceiling. This is fixture F6's shape, which the cost model still prices
// — the two are not in conflict, and the split is deliberate: `fire()` bounds SHAPES and
// check_landings bounds TIME, so a shape whose cost is a fact worth pinning can still be
// unplaceable.
//
// And it is unplaceable, structurally rather than by a poor choice of spin. The combined
// span from the first op's write to the second's is 116 cycles against a blanking window
// measured at 122.9 (116 and not the pre-Tier-3-item-1 120: the two CRAM words got 4
// cycles cheaper each, which is nowhere near the 30 cycles of margin this shape is short
// by, so the poison is red for the same structural reason as before) (docs/benchmarks/scanline-p2/HBLANK-WINDOW-SWEEP-RESULTS.md), so no
// centring leaves either margin. This is the poison for the sentence in `fire()`'s
// stream-op ceiling that says a second stream op has no legal placement.
//
// TWO DIAGNOSTICS, AND THE COUNT IS HALF THE ASSERTION. The solver centres the COMBINED
// span, which pushes op 0 before the window opens (EARLY) and leaves op 1 finishing after
// it closes (LATE) — one report each, from opposite edges of the same guard. A count of 1
// would mean the solver stopped centring the pair and started treating them independently,
// which is the design mistake this fixture exists to keep out.
//
// NO IMPORTS, like every ordinary author's module: raster_dsl and engine.vdp are
// COMPTIME_HELPERS members, glob-injected into every module by the real build. See
// the README on why the lane cannot reproduce that injection yet.
module games.sonic4.test.poison.poison_landing_early

const POISON_LANDING_EARLY = [
    fire(100, [stream_cram($22, [$0EEE]), stream_cram($26, [$0AAA])]),
]

// THE ELABORATION HOOK — see poison_four_bands.emp's note. Trivially-true predicate;
// the diagnostic under test comes from inside the call.
ensure(raster_program(POISON_LANDING_EARLY).len > 0,
       "poison_landing_early: raster_program returned nothing — this poison no longer reaches the guard it targets")
